//! Spec: `learn` over a document runs every stage as one recorded run -
//! the policy resolved once and recorded, the source captured, tasks
//! generated by the policy and admitted by code, each solved and graded by
//! its kind's verifier, a failure critiqued and retried, and the passing
//! answers written as an sft-final dataset the trainer's own parser
//! accepts - hands that dataset to training, and puts the candidate
//! through the release gate, which releases nothing it cannot measure.
//! The release `policy:default` resolved to when the run started is the
//! one the whole run uses, however the alias moves. `--dry-run` writes
//! nothing.
//!
//! The policy is a scripted in-test model and code runs in the process
//! sandbox; training is a test double, since training needs weights.

// Helpers outside a #[test] fn unwrap too: a panic is the failure report.
#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used)]

